<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>The single re-evaluating scheduled job</title>
    <phase>3 Evaluator and Signal lifecycle</phase>
    <gate>030 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Background workload placement decision plus the mechanism that prevents the worklist rotting.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Follows ADR-036 with six live reference implementations.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Tasks 032, 033 and 034 all attach to this job.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030,003</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,scheduled-job,signals</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build ONE re-evaluating scheduled job that upserts Signals whose predicate now holds and closes those whose predicate no longer holds, in one pass.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer. One component deciding both directions.</role>
  <goal>A nightly ADR-036 IScheduledJob that re-evaluates every enabled policy and both creates and closes Signals, stamping sprk_lastevaluated on everything it touches.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Path B window is relative to now, so the predicate truth value changes even when nobody writes anything. Of four state transitions, TWO have no event to hook: death by time (the communication ages out) and birth by time (an old budget revision ages out, re-truthing the notExists half). So the nightly pass cannot be closure-only, and event-driven evaluation alone would never fire ConditionCleared.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJob.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/SecureRecordIsolationCensusJob.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/RegistrationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Scope: implement IScheduledJob. NO new hand-rolled timer BackgroundService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052">Scope: this workload runs in the BFF. Tie-breaker is fewer moving parts; the workload is hundreds of rows, not a scale problem. State the placement decision in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ONE component that both creates and closes. Do NOT build an evaluator plus a separate sweep: two components can disagree about the same Signal, which miscounts suppression in both directions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: cadence derives from the EXISTING sprk_lane column. Decide-lane policies run here AND on the event triggers; Do-lane policies run here ONLY. Do not add a per-policy trigger column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: stamp sprk_lastevaluated on every Signal the pass touches, so a stale Signal is distinguishable from an unevaluated one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: if this task changes src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api, state the Placement Justification in the PR citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, and measure publish size against a FRESH build of master from a short path with file counts compared on both sides. Ceiling 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: any test this task adds that asserts a Dataverse column list, entity name or option-set value must be paired with something touching the real schema. A consistently throwing path is a defect to diagnose, never noise to tolerate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: before opening a BFF PR, run /conflict-check. 56 of 62 active projects declare a hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">OWNER DECISION 2026-10-04: no silent failure. The writer fails closed by design, so a broken credential, a refused privilege or a dead job would otherwise look exactly like 'no conditions found'. The evaluator therefore (a) emits an App Insights custom metric per run (ontology.evaluator.runs, dimension outcome = succeeded|failed, plus signals written/updated/closed counts), following the existing custom-metric pattern the alerts in infrastructure/bicep/modules/alerts.bicep consume; (b) logs every writer refusal (credential, token, privilege, escalation) at Error with a stable EventId and increments ontology.writer.failures (dimension reason); (c) records the time of the last SUCCESSFUL run and exposes it on a DIAGNOSTIC health check tagged so it lands on /healthz/catalog-style diagnostics, NOT on the /healthz liveness probe (a stale evaluator must not recycle instances).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">FROM TASK 030 REVIEW R13 (2026-10-04): the Signal writer does NOT set sprk_regardingrecordnumber (ADR-024 resolver set) or sprk_privilegeflagged (schema draft: 'copied forward', ADR-015), and no spec line assigns either to task 030. Decide here, with a spec citation, whether the evaluator supplies them (e.g. privilegeflagged copied from the subject when the Signal is built) and pass them to the writer; if neither belongs to this task, record which task owns them. A privilege flag that silently stays empty is the kind of gap ADR-015 exists to prevent. Details: notes/030-signal-writer-progress.md.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Scheduled background jobs</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Scheduled census job" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/SecureRecordIsolationCensusJob.cs">The nearest shape in the repo: a scheduled pass over many rows producing a reconciliation outcome. Copy its registration and lease handling.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Read SecureRecordIsolationCensusJob and one other IScheduledJob to establish the registration, lease and logging conventions.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the job: for each enabled policy, compile its body (task 021), run it, and upsert a Signal per hit via the writer (task 030).</step>
    <step order="3">In the SAME pass, for each still-open Signal of that policy, re-evaluate its predicate and close it if it no longer holds (task 033 supplies the closure semantics).</step>
    <step order="4">Stamp sprk_lastevaluated on every Signal touched, created or not.</step>
    <step order="5">Derive cadence from sprk_lane: process both lanes here.</step>
    <step order="6">Register the job and confirm it appears in the admin jobs endpoint.</step>
    <step order="7">Add tests: a policy that now holds creates a Signal; a Signal whose predicate stopped holding is closed; a Signal still holding is left open with a refreshed sprk_lastevaluated.</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="9">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a full nightly re-evaluation proves too expensive at realistic data volumes, STOP and escalate to agree a scoping strategy rather than silently narrowing the pass to recently-changed rows. Narrowing it reintroduces the birth-by-time blind spot that this design exists to close.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Six IScheduledJob implementations exist, but none evaluates policies or manages Signal lifecycle.</existing>
    <extension>No. The existing jobs are domain-specific reconciliations; this is a new workload. The ADR-036 seam itself IS being reused rather than a new scheduling mechanism built.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Nothing closes a Signal when its condition clears on its own, so the worklist fills with stale items, users mute it, and suppression miscounts because an auto-cleared Signal is indistinguishable from a human dismissal.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJob.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/RegistrationModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJobTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an enabled policy whose predicate now holds for a matter, when the job runs, then a Signal exists for it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an open Signal whose predicate no longer holds, when the job runs, then it is closed with a resolution type and no Decision Record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an open Signal whose predicate still holds, when the job runs, then it stays open and sprk_lastevaluated is refreshed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Do-lane policy, when the job runs, then it is evaluated (both lanes run nightly).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a disabled policy is not evaluated at all.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the job is an IScheduledJob and no new timer BackgroundService was added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The job is registered and visible via the admin jobs endpoint.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All tests pass; the BFF builds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the writer refuses (e.g. empty writer client id), when the job runs, then the run is recorded with outcome=failed, an Error log carries the stable EventId, and ontology.writer.failures increments; it is never recorded as a successful run with zero Signals.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given no successful run for longer than the threshold, when the diagnostic health check is read, then it reports Unhealthy with the last-success time, and /healthz (liveness) is unaffected.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-11, FR-12 and FR-15. design.md section 8.3 carries the reasoning, including the four-transition table. The ADR-040 amendment (task 003) must be merged before or alongside this task.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
